// data/ai_configs/mimic_ai.tres: Dormant -> Awaken (on hit) -> HoldAction / MimicBite / MimicGrab.
//
// The five-state graph reduces to a mode plus two scored attacks:
//  - Dormant mode until the first hit.
//  - Awaken -> HoldAction on AnimationFinished never fires in Godot (nothing ever sets that flag), so the
//    "wake animation delay" doesn't exist and Awaken is just normal combat: range checks and all.
//  - MimicBite (HEAVY) while within 18, MimicGrab (LIGHT) while within 28, otherwise HoldAction (nothing).
//    Both states emit their command every frame -- hence cooldown 0. Bite is listed with the higher weight
//    so that where both reach (inside 18) it bites, as the source's transition order does.
//  - No Chase state: the Mimic is immobile.
//  - TargetDead -> HoldAction is handled generically (a dead target is no target).
//  - detect_range = 0.0 in the .tres (and is never read); no gate here.
{
  "start_mode": "dormant",
  "approach": false,
  "attacks": [
    { "command": "heavy", "range": 18.0, "weight": 2.0 },   // MimicBite   -> mimic_attack
    { "command": "light", "range": 28.0, "weight": 1.0 }    // MimicGrab   -> mimic_grab
  ]
}
